y without alarm signs like weight loss or mass effect", "Isolated infectious etiology: inconsistent with lifelong recurrence pattern", "Congenital heart defect complication (e.g. Eisenmenger syndrome): inconsistent with current symptoms and imaging findings"], "alarm_features": ["Chronic multisystem involvement (respiratory + sinus + growth)", "Persistent failure to thrive trajectory", "Structural airway abnormality on MRI"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Cystic Fibrosis and Other Genetic Pulmonary Disorders", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.5017148780382045, "posterior": 0.5355646736113817, "danger": 0.2, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Recurrent infections without rare pathogens or systemic compromise weakly reduces immunodeficiency likelihood."], "evidence_against": ["Tricuspid stenosis is a known cardiac finding in cystic fibrosis, but the LR- suggests only minor reduction in diagnostic likelihood."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Chronic Inflammatory Airway Diseases", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.07, "danger": 0.1, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Structural airway dilation moderately disfavors (LR- 0.3529) chronic inflammatory diseases as the primary mechanism."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Immunodeficiency Syndromes with Recurrent Infections", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.039, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Recurrent infections without rare pathogens or systemic compromise weakly reduces immunodeficiency likelihood."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Developmental/Structural Airway Abnormalities", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.029, "danger": 0.05, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Cystic Fibrosis with Recurrent Sinopulmonary Infections", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.40141154801555273, "posterior": 0.4702802301405653, "danger": 0.2, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Tricuspid stenosis and airway dilation provide moderate evidence for CF (LR+ 3.6667), but growth percentile weakly reduces it."], "evidence_against": ["Normal growth trajectory without pancreatic issues weakly reduces (LR- 0.5294) CF likelihood but does not exclude it."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia with Chronic Airway Dysfunction", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.058, "danger": 0.1, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of ciliary abnormalities on MRI weakly disfavors (LR- 0.5882) PCD but does not eliminate it due to variable imaging presentation."]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Alpha-1 Antitrypsin Deficiency with Pulmonary Involvement", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.007, "danger": 0.05, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of liver disease/emphysema reduces A1AD likelihood but does not eliminate it in pediatric patients."]}}, "frontier": ["B1.1", "B1.1"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the MRI demonstration of airway dilation and the history of tricuspid stenosis support cystic fibrosis (CF) as the most likely diagnosis?", "summary": "Tricuspid stenosis and airway dilation provide moderate evidence for CF (LR+ 3.6667), but growth percentile weakly reduces it."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the structural airway dilation findings on MRI more consistent with primary ciliary dyskinesia (PCD) than with cystic fibrosis (CF) in this patient?", "summary": "MRI findings slightly favor PCD over CF (LR+ 3.3333), but absence of ciliary abnormalities weakly disfavors PCD."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the patient's lifelong chronic cough and sinus infections with structural airway dilation more consistent with chronic inflammation than with developmental/structural processes?", "summary": "Chronic symptoms and structural findings moderately disfavor (LR- 0.3529) chronic inflammatory diseases as the primary mechanism."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the patient's maintained 25th percentile growth without pancreatic insufficiency disfavor cystic fibrosis (CF) despite the structural airway findings?", "summary": "Normal growth trajectory without pancreatic issues weakly reduces (LR- 0.5294) CF likelihood but does not exclude it."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of ciliary structure abnormalities on MRI disfavor primary ciliary dyskinesia (PCD) as the underlying diagnosis?", "summary": "Lack of ciliary abnormalities on MRI weakly disfavors (LR- 0.5882) PCD but does not eliminate it due to variable imaging presentation."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the MRI finding of structural airway dilation disfavor chronic inflammatory airway diseases as the primary mechanism for this patient's symptoms?", "summary": "Structural airway dilation moderately disfavors (LR- 0.3529) chronic inflammatory diseases as the primary mechanism."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B1", 0.578], ["B1.1", 0.45], ["B2", 0.271]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.502], ["B1.1", 0.401], ["B2", 0.107]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.536], ["B1.1", 0.47], ["B2", 0.07]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No immediate life-threatening instability markers (airway, breathing, circulation) are present. Vitals suggest borderline hypotension (90/58 mmHg) and tachycardia (120 bpm), but no end-organ compromise or acute respiratory failure. No time-critical syndrome patterns (e.g., septic shock, tension pneumothorax) are confirmed by current evidence.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading terminal branch (B1.1) posterior (0.47) <0.75; actionable_parent_syndrome not triggered as B1's children (B1.1, B1.2) have divergent diagnostic paths (CF vs PCD); info_exhaustion not met since sweat chloride testing (key CF discriminator) remains untried despite being requestable"}, "turn_budget_used": 3, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.65, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.4702802301405653, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following findings is associated with this patient's most likely underlying diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Diastolic murmur best heard along the right lower sternal border"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Hypocalcemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Increased chloride in the patient's sweat"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Repeat sinus infections secondary to seasonal allergies"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Social withdrawal and avoidance of eye contact"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Recurrent opportunistic infections', 'Immunodeficiency', 'Episodic upper airway obstruction'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "program_faults": [], "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.578}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B1.1", "label": "Cystic Fibrosis with Recurrent Sinopulmonary Infections", "posterior": 0.47, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 2, "disconfirming": 3, "last_disconfirming_digest": "Normal growth trajectory without pancreatic issues weakly reduces (LR- 0.5294) CF likelihood but does not exclude it."}, "action_intents": [{"t": 3, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B2", "B1.2"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=25%, source=primekg]\n\nNOT typically seen in Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia with Chronic Airway Dysfunction: abnormal axonemal organization of respiratory motile cilia, abnormal sweat electrolytes, decreased fertility, heterotaxy\n\nRelated to Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia with Chronic Airway Dysfunction: ciliary discoordination due to random ciliary orientation, ciliary dyskinesia with defective radial spokes, ciliary dyskinesia with excessively long cilia\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  A 10-year-old girl is admitted to the medical floor for a respiratory infection → recurrent upper respiratory tract infections → Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia with Chronic Airway Dysfunction\n  A 10-year-old girl is admitted to the medical floor for a respiratory infection → recurrent lower respiratory tract infections → Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia with Chronic Airway Dysfunction\n  A 10-year-old girl is admitted to the medical floor for a respiratory infection → recurrent respiratory infections → Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia with Chronic Airway Dysfunction"}
